a86e9c62-7ad5-4bb8-b95b-6367c0a645ce	bfd3b7bd-44e6-43f6-97bd-071a844d2065	0	INFOSYS LIMITED\nAnnual Report\nFiscal Year 2023 (Year ended\nMarch 31, 2023)\nIndustry-leading growth, resilient margins, and continued investment in digital, cloud and\ngenerative AI capabilities for our clients worldwide.\n$18,212\nMn$2,983 Mn21.0%Rs. 34.00\nTotal Revenue (FY23)Net Profit (FY23)Operating MarginDividend / Share\n\nInfosys Limited | Annual Report FY2023Year ended March 31, 2023\nPage 1\nContents\n1. Message from the CEO & MD\n2. Message from the CFO\n3. FY2023 Performance at a Glance\n4. Financial Statements   Statement of Comprehensive Income\n5. Financial Statements   Balance Sheet\n6. Capital Allocation & Shareholder Returns\n7. Segment & Geographic Highlights\n8. Client Partnerships & Key Wins\n9. People, Culture & ESG\n10. Awards & Industry Recognition\n11. Corporate Governance & Board of Directors\n12. Outlook   FY2024 Guidance\n13. Safe Harbor Statement\n\nInfosys Limited | Annual Report FY2023Year ended March 31, 2023\nPage 2\n1. Message from the CEO & MD\nFiscal  2023  was  a  year  of  industry-leading  growth  for  Infosys,  delivered  against  a  complex  macroeconomic\nbackdrop.  Our  continued  focus  on  digital,  cloud  and  automation  capabilities  resonated  strongly  with  clients,\nand we launched new programs leveraging generative AI platforms to help clients unlock further value.\n Our  strong  performance  in  FY23  is  a  testimony  to  the  continued  focus  on  digital,  cloud  and\nautomation  capabilities  which  resonated  with  our  clients.  We  have  launched	1	General	2026-09-19 17:23:24.460609
9d559d55-a259-4b0e-a34c-c4cc46d18aa2	bfd3b7bd-44e6-43f6-97bd-071a844d2065	1	er value.\n Our  strong  performance  in  FY23  is  a  testimony  to  the  continued  focus  on  digital,  cloud  and\nautomation  capabilities  which  resonated  with  our  clients.  We  have  launched  exciting  programs  with\nour  clients  leveraging  generative  AI  platforms.  As  the  environment  has  changed,  we  see  strong\ninterest from our clients for efficiency, cost and consolidation opportunities, resulting in a strong large\ndeal pipeline. We have expanded our internal program on efficiency and cost to build a path to higher\nmargins in the medium term. We continue to invest in our people and in supporting our clients. \n  Salil Parekh, Chief Executive Officer & Managing Director\nRevenue  for  the  year  grew  15.4%  in  constant  currency  terms,  with  large  deal  total  contract  value  of  $9.8\nbillion  for  the  full  year,  and  digital  revenues     now  62.2%  of  the  overall  business     growing  25.6%  in\nconstant currency. The Board has proposed a final dividend for the year and the Company completed a share\nbuyback during the period, underscoring continued commitment to disciplined capital allocation.\n\nInfosys Limited | Annual Report FY2023Year ended March 31, 2023\nPage 3\n2. Message from the CFO\nFY2023  operating  margins  held  firm  at  21.0%  despite  wage  inflation,  cross-currency  headwinds  and  a\nchallenging demand environment in parts of the year. Continued cost optimization and operational efficiency\nprograms  supported  margin  resilience	1	General	2026-09-19 17:23:24.460609
84da3e54-115c-44a0-a19b-a25e4e6aa00c	bfd3b7bd-44e6-43f6-97bd-071a844d2065	2	 wage  inflation,  cross-currency  headwinds  and  a\nchallenging demand environment in parts of the year. Continued cost optimization and operational efficiency\nprograms  supported  margin  resilience,  while  collections  discipline  drove  strong  free  cash  flow  generation,\nparticularly in the fourth quarter.\n Our  continued  focus  on  cost  optimization  and  operational  efficiencies  have  helped  in  achieving\noperating  margins  of  21.0%  in  FY23.  Free  cash  generation  in  Q4,  led  by  robust  collections,  was\nstrong. Executing on our capital allocation policy, we successfully completed the share buyback and\nhave proposed a final dividend of Rs. 17.50 for FY23. \n  Nilanjan Roy, Chief Financial Officer\nFull-year free cash flow was $2,534 million, representing 85.0% conversion of net profit. Basic earnings per\nshare  for  the  year  stood  at  $0.71,  with  EPS  growth  of  9.7%  in  rupee  terms  for  FY23,  reflecting  steady\nprofitability even as the Company invested in talent, infrastructure and generative AI capability-building.\n\nInfosys Limited | Annual Report FY2023Year ended March 31, 2023\nPage 4\n3. FY2023 Performance at a Glance\nFor  the  year  ended  March  31,  2023,  Infosys  delivered  broad-based  growth  across  industry  verticals  and\ngeographies, with the following headline metrics (IFRS, USD, unless noted):\n$18,212\nMn\nTotal Revenue\n(+11.7% YoY reported)\n15.4%\nRevenue Growth\n(Constant Currency)\n21.0%\nOperating Margin\n$2,983 Mn\nNet Profit\n(bef	1	General	2026-09-19 17:23:24.460609
