b9c13469-1599-4f03-a56d-2ce79b5d2474	bfd3b7bd-44e6-43f6-97bd-071a844d2065	5	obligations292288\nOther current liabilities and provisions3,1352,766\nTotal current liabilities4,7694,433\nLease liabilities (non-current)859607\nOther non-current liabilities460521\nTotal non-current liabilities1,3191,128\nTotal liabilities6,0885,561\nTotal equity attributable to shareholders9,1729,941\nNon-controlling interests5253\nTotal equity9,2249,994\n\nInfosys Limited | Annual Report FY2023Year ended March 31, 2023\nPage 7\nParticularsMar 31, 2023Mar 31, 2022\nTotal liabilities and equity15,31215,555\n\nInfosys Limited | Annual Report FY2023Year ended March 31, 2023\nPage 8\n6. Capital Allocation & Shareholder Returns\nFor FY2023, the Board recommended a final dividend of Rs. 17.50 per share ($0.21 per ADS), which together\nwith the interim dividend of Rs. 16.50 per share already paid, brings the total dividend per share for FY23 to\nRs. 34.00 (approx. $0.41 per ADS)   a 9.7% increase over FY22. This amounts to a total dividend payout of\napproximately Rs. 14,200 crore (approx. $1.7 billion) for the year.\nThe  Company  completed  its  open-market  share  buyback  on  February  13,  2023,  at  an  average  price  of\napproximately  Rs.  1,539  per  share  (against  a  maximum  buyback  price  of  Rs.  1,850  per  share),  reducing\nshare capital by 1.44%.\nIncluding  the  concluded  buyback  and  the  FY23  final  dividend,  Infosys  returned  approximately  86%  of  Free\nCash Flow to shareholders under its current capital allocation policy.\nCapital Allocation MetricFY23 Value\nInterim dividen	2	General	2026-09-19 17:23:24.460609
70fa8437-2b11-4fec-9a99-d00fcc977e88	bfd3b7bd-44e6-43f6-97bd-071a844d2065	6	 the  FY23  final  dividend,  Infosys  returned  approximately  86%  of  Free\nCash Flow to shareholders under its current capital allocation policy.\nCapital Allocation MetricFY23 Value\nInterim dividend per share (paid)Rs. 16.50\nFinal dividend per share (proposed)Rs. 17.50\nTotal dividend per share, FY23Rs. 34.00 (+9.7% YoY)\nTotal dividend payout, FY23~Rs. 14,200 crore (~$1.7 Bn)\nShare buyback completion dateFebruary 13, 2023\nAverage buyback price~Rs. 1,539 per share\nReduction in share capital from buyback1.44%\nFCF returned to shareholders (buyback + dividend)~86%\n\nInfosys Limited | Annual Report FY2023Year ended March 31, 2023\nPage 9\n7. Segment & Geographic Highlights\nGrowth in FY2023 was broad-based across industry verticals and geographical regions, supported by strong\nlarge-deal momentum and continued client demand for digital, cloud and cost-efficiency programs.\n \nDigital revenues comprised 62.2% of overall revenue, growing 25.6% year-on-year in constant currency.\n \nFull-year large deal Total Contract Value (TCV) reached $9.8 billion, with $2.1 billion signed in Q4 alone.\n \nQ4 FY23 revenue grew 8.8% year-on-year in constant currency, with a 3.2% sequential decline reflecting\nseasonal softness.\n \nQ4 operating margin held at 21.0%, matching the full-year average, with free cash flow conversion of 95.7%\nfor the quarter.\n\nInfosys Limited | Annual Report FY2023Year ended March 31, 2023\nPage 10\n8. Client Partnerships & Key Wins\nInfosys  deepened  strategic  partnerships  across 	3	General	2026-09-19 17:23:24.460609
a7f84f2f-4c6c-4e06-b61f-2b72e34a81b5	bfd3b7bd-44e6-43f6-97bd-071a844d2065	7	flow conversion of 95.7%\nfor the quarter.\n\nInfosys Limited | Annual Report FY2023Year ended March 31, 2023\nPage 10\n8. Client Partnerships & Key Wins\nInfosys  deepened  strategic  partnerships  across  energy,  technology,  manufacturing,  banking  and  the  public\nsector during FY2023. Selected highlights:\n \nbp: Collaborated to create an 'Energy-as-a-Service' offering for holistic energy management, supporting\nsavings, decarbonization and supply reliability.\n \nMicrosoft: Extended a two-decade collaboration to accelerate cloud adoption through Microsoft\nAzure-powered solutions integrated with Infosys Cobalt.\n \nHPE: Rolled out Private 5G-as-a-Service, combining HPE's Private 5G solutions with Infosys' pre-integrated\nvertical use cases.\n \nZF Friedrichshafen AG: Revamped a multi-echelon supply chain using SAP Integrated Business Planning\nand Infosys Cobalt.\n \nABN AMRO: Implemented the Infosys Finacle Liquidity Management Solution for corporate treasury\ncustomers.\n \nUNDP: Deployed the Quantum Global Digital Management System via Infosys Public Services for a unified\nplatform across UN development operations.\n \nGE Digital: Partnered to accelerate grid transformation and IT-OT alignment for utilities clients.\n \nStarHub: Infosys Compaz supported an IT transformation to improve platform performance, customer\nsatisfaction and cyber resilience.\n\nInfosys Limited | Annual Report FY2023Year ended March 31, 2023\nPage 11\n9. People, Culture & ESG\nInfosys  continued  to  invest  in  its  workf	3	General	2026-09-19 17:23:24.460609
9529a1ea-4b86-480a-9a5c-77f1f34e54d8	bfd3b7bd-44e6-43f6-97bd-071a844d2065	8	erformance, customer\nsatisfaction and cyber resilience.\n\nInfosys Limited | Annual Report FY2023Year ended March 31, 2023\nPage 11\n9. People, Culture & ESG\nInfosys  continued  to  invest  in  its  workforce  and  sustainability  agenda  through  FY2023,  with  over  300,000\nemployees  globally  supporting  clients  across  more  than  50  countries.  Attrition  trended  lower  through  the\nsecond half of the year as demand-side hiring normalized industry-wide.\n \nRecognized as one of the 2023 World's Most Ethical Companies  by Ethisphere.\n \nPositioned in the Leadership category of the Indian Corporate Governance Scorecard Assessment 2023.\n \nRecognized as a Global Top Employer 2023 by the Top Employers Institute.\n \nWon the Sustainability 100+ Award for Carbon Neutrality under the Climate Action category.\n \nWon the Economic Times Best Organisations for Women Award, 2023.\n \nWon the Asset Triple A ESG Awards 2022 for Diversity and Inclusion.\nInfosys  remains  committed  to  being  a  well-governed,  environmentally  sustainable  organization  in  which\ndiverse talent thrives in an inclusive workplace, aligned with its long-standing carbon neutrality commitments\nand skilling initiatives.\n\nInfosys Limited | Annual Report FY2023Year ended March 31, 2023\nPage 12\n10. Awards & Industry Recognition\nIndependent  analyst  firms  and  industry  bodies  recognized  Infosys  as  a  leader  across  multiple  service  lines\nand geographies during FY2023, including:\n \nLeader   2022 ISG Provider Le	3	General	2026-09-19 17:23:24.460609
0a60d911-59aa-4347-b707-3e41db6faf41	bfd3b7bd-44e6-43f6-97bd-071a844d2065	9	ition\nIndependent  analyst  firms  and  industry  bodies  recognized  Infosys  as  a  leader  across  multiple  service  lines\nand geographies during FY2023, including:\n \nLeader   2022 ISG Provider Lens  Digital Business Enablement and ESG Services (US, UK, Nordics,\nGermany, Australia, Brazil).\n \nLeader   Forrester Wave : Multicloud-Managed Services Providers, Q1 2023.\n \nLeader   Everest Group PEAK Matrix  Assessments across Advanced Analytics & Insights, Digital\nTransformation Consulting, and Life & Annuity Insurance ADS (2023).\n \nLeader   IDC MarketScape assessments in Manufacturing Intelligence Transformation and Intelligent Digital\nWorkplace Services (Asia/Pacific), 2023.\n \nLeader   HFS Horizons for Retail Banking Services, Digital Engineering Services, and Metaverse Services\nProviders, 2023.\n \nLeader   NelsonHall Financial Services Cloud, BPaaS and SaaS NEAT assessments, 2023.\n \nInfosys BPM recognized as Leader & Star Performer, Everest Group Capital Markets Operations PEAK\nMatrix  2023.\n\nInfosys Limited | Annual Report FY2023Year ended March 31, 2023\nPage 13\n11. Corporate Governance & Leadership\nInfosys'  governance  framework  is  built  around  an  independent,  majority  non-executive  Board,  robust  risk\noversight,  and  strong  disclosure  practices     reflected  in  its  Leadership-category  placement  in  the  Indian\nCorporate Governance Scorecard Assessment 2023.\nName / BodyRole\nSalil ParekhChief Executive Officer & Managing Director\nNilanjan RoyChief Financia	4	General	2026-09-19 17:23:24.460609
