15818486-0eec-458b-97cb-3dae2d224621	6839aabd-420f-4a23-b2d4-35b1871b5ed8	3	ency and macroeconomic risk. As a company with substantial cross-border operations, results are exposed\nto movements in the US dollar, euro, and other currencies relative to the Indian rupee, as well as to global\nmacroeconomic conditions affecting client IT budgets.\nEffective tax rate risk. The effective tax rate for the quarter was 22.2% after favorable adjustments; management\nguided a normalized effective tax rate range of 29% to 30% for the following fiscal year, indicating potential upward\npressure on the tax rate.\nWage inflation and talent cost risk. Employee benefit expenses represented the largest single cost line (Rs.\n82,620 crore, roughly 54% of revenue), making the business sensitive to wage inflation and talent retention costs in\na competitive IT labor market.\n6. Forward Guidance (as issued with FY2024 results)\nFY2025 revenue growth guidance\n(constant currency)\n1% to 3%\nFY2025 operating margin guidance20% to 22%\nEnd of FY2024 Annual Financial Research Summary. Source filings: Infosys Limited Form 6-K submissions to the U.S. Securities and\nExchange Commission and Infosys quarterly/annual earnings press releases, fiscal year ended March 31, 2024.	2	General	2026-09-19 18:06:38.508372
